From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sun, 15 Nov 2026 20:20:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] tcg/wasm32: make the JIT threshold adjustable at run time

INSTANTIATE_NUM (1500) decides after how many interpreted executions a
TB is compiled to its own Wasm module.  Turn it into a variable with an
exported setter, porty_set_jit_threshold(), so the page can run a guest
with the Wasm code generator effectively off (interpreter only) or on
for every TB, without rebuilding.  That is what separates code-generator
bugs from bugs elsewhere when a guest misbehaves.
---
diff --git a/tcg/wasm32.c b/tcg/wasm32.c
index d60ce4b..5095aeb 100644
--- a/tcg/wasm32.c
+++ b/tcg/wasm32.c
@@ -30,6 +30,21 @@
 #include <emscripten/threading.h>
 #include "wasm32.h"
 
+int porty_jit_threshold = INSTANTIATE_NUM_DEFAULT;
+
+/*
+ * Porty: set how many times a TB runs in the interpreter before it is
+ * compiled to Wasm.  0 compiles every TB on first use; 2147483647 in effect
+ * never compiles (interpreter only); a negative value restores the default.
+ * Returns the value in effect.  The page calls this from
+ * onRuntimeInitialized, before main() starts any vCPU.
+ */
+EMSCRIPTEN_KEEPALIVE int porty_set_jit_threshold(int n)
+{
+    porty_jit_threshold = n < 0 ? INSTANTIATE_NUM_DEFAULT : n;
+    return porty_jit_threshold;
+}
+
 __thread uintptr_t tci_tb_ptr;
 
 /* Disassemble TCI bytecode. */
diff --git a/tcg/wasm32.h b/tcg/wasm32.h
index 82ac7e3..8d493a1 100644
--- a/tcg/wasm32.h
+++ b/tcg/wasm32.h
@@ -37,6 +37,14 @@ int get_core_nums();
 
 void init_wasm32();
 
-#define INSTANTIATE_NUM 1500
+/*
+ * Executions of a TB before it is compiled to its own Wasm module (until
+ * then TCI interprets it).  Porty: a variable rather than a constant, so the
+ * page can change it (?jit=) to tell bugs in the Wasm code generator from
+ * bugs elsewhere; see porty_set_jit_threshold() in wasm32.c.
+ */
+#define INSTANTIATE_NUM_DEFAULT 1500
+extern int porty_jit_threshold;
+#define INSTANTIATE_NUM porty_jit_threshold
 
 #endif
